    <statement><p>Write a triple integral, including limits of
integration, that gives the volume between
<m>x+5y+z = 1</m> and <m>3x+7y+z = 1</m> and above
<m>x+y\le 2, x\ge 0, y\ge 0</m>.</p>
<p>volume = <m>\int_a^b\int_c^d\int_e^f</m><fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0001"/>
<m>d</m><fillin characters="3" name="AnSwEr0002"/> <m>d</m><fillin characters="3" name="AnSwEr0003"/>
<m>d</m><fillin characters="3" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
<p>where
<m>a =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0005"/>,
<m>b =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0006"/>,</p>
<p><m>c =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0007"/>,
<m>d =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0008"/>,</p>
<p><m>e =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0009"/>, and
<m>f =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0010"/>.</p>
<p>(Note: values for all answer blanks must be supplied for
this problem to be able to check the answers provided.)</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>z</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>y</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
