        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2-x</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1-3x-7y</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>1-1x-5y</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>z = 1-x-5y</me>
and
<me>z = 1-3x-7y.</me>

For <m>x,y\ge0</m>, the plane <m>z=1-x-5y</m> is above <m>z=1-3x-7y</m>.  The region
in the <m>xy</m>-plane is the triangular region under <m>y = 2-x</m>,
above the <m>x</m>-axis and to the right of the <m>y</m>-axis.  Thus the
volume is
<me>V = \int_0^{2}\int_0^{2-x}\int_{1-3x-7y}^{1-x-5y}1\,dz\,dy\,dx.</me>
The order of integration of <m>x</m> and <m>y</m> can be reversed, giving
<me>V = \int_0^{2}\int_0^{2-y}\int_{1-3x-7y}^{1-x-5y}1\,dz\,dx\,dy.</me>



</solution>
